<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mikhail Skobelev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1843–1882</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mikhail Skobelev was a Russian general famous for his campaigns in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>. He crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kokand">Kokand</a> rising of 1875–76 and became the first governor of the Fergana Oblast, then won fame at Plevna and Shipka-Sheinovo in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1877-1878">Russo-Turkish War</a> of 1877–78. In 1881 he stormed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> fortress of Geok Tepe. He died suddenly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> at the age of 38.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mikhail-skobelev.jpg" alt="Mikhail Skobelev" width="320" height="494" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sergey Lvovich Levitsky · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skobelev,_Michel,_par_Serge_Levitsky,_BNF_Gallica.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
